{"content":[{"c":["RAKKATH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of 19 cities allotted to Naphtali’s tribe for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.35","r":"Josh.19.35","rawR":"Josh.19.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.35","value":"Josh.19.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:35"},"). The city served as a buffer against military attack on the western shore of the Sea of Galilee. Jewish tradition identifies Rakkath with Tiberias, but modern scholars prefer its location at either Khirbet el-Quneitireh or Tell Eklatiyah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Rakkath","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.35","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.35","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.35"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b869b486a59b1145abfa1fa2c69e2a24e8dba9ee4342821c6f8f3b7d6a5e8bba","sourceItemName":"Rakkath","sourceItemOrder":30,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rakkath","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Rakkath","title":"Rakkath","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}